WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.439
Hi, I'm Tungsten!

00:00:02.439 --> 00:00:07.417
Let me show you the two numerical tricks inside DeepSeek's matrix multiply library.

00:00:09.017 --> 00:00:13.061
Give every run of a hundred and twenty eight elements its own

00:00:13.061 --> 00:00:17.443
scale, and empty the tensor core's accumulator into wider registers just as often.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:22.256
With one scale for the whole tensor, the largest value sets it,

00:00:22.256 --> 00:00:25.332
and the quiet values sink toward the bottom of the format.

00:00:25.753 --> 00:00:29.819
With one scale for every group, an outlier only spoils its own neighbours.

00:00:29.819 --> 00:00:33.573
The price is that the scale now changes inside the dot product.

00:00:35.258 --> 00:00:38.932
One warp does nothing but issue copies, pulling the next tile of

00:00:38.932 --> 00:00:40.769
activations and weights toward the chip.

00:00:41.189 --> 00:00:44.466
The tiles land in shared memory a stage ahead, so the maths

00:00:44.466 --> 00:00:45.558
never waits on memory.

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:50.171
The tensor core multiplies them, accumulating in a register that keeps

00:00:50.171 --> 00:00:51.695
only about fourteen bits.

00:00:52.115 --> 00:00:56.007
Every hundred and twenty eight elements the partial sum is handed to

00:00:56.007 --> 00:00:59.250
the CUDA cores, scaled there, and added in full precision.

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:03.275
Two groups of maths warps take turns, so one is adding while

00:01:03.275 --> 00:01:05.978
the other multiplies, and the tensor cores never idle.

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:10.251
This is the number the whole design turns on.

00:01:10.251 --> 00:01:13.034
Fourteen bits, where the output format has twenty four.

00:01:14.592 --> 00:01:17.928
The loading warps keep three copies in flight at once, each issue

00:01:17.928 --> 00:01:19.318
overlapping the one before it.

00:01:19.738 --> 00:01:24.208
Below them the two maths groups alternate: multiply, then promote, staggered so

00:01:24.208 --> 00:01:25.697
the two never collide.

00:01:27.183 --> 00:01:31.734
The hand-written assembly patch lasted about a year before the compiler absorbed it.

00:01:31.734 --> 00:01:34.535
The numerics underneath are still the whole design.

00:01:36.108 --> 00:01:39.844
A scale for every group, a promotion to wider adds, and warps

00:01:39.844 --> 00:01:41.089
arranged so nothing waits.

00:01:41.509 --> 00:01:43.688
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:43.688 --> 00:01:44.311
I'm Tungsten.

00:01:44.311 --> 00:01:44.622
Bye!
